s all other Class A common stock and are considered to be issued and outstanding. The following table summarizes the activity for the nine months ended September 30, 2026:\nL2081: __________\nL2082: \nL2083: (1) Includes c ash and cas h equivalents, restricted cash, segregated cash, cash equivalents, and securities under federal and other regulations, deposits with clearing organizations, and investments.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nhood-20260930 (https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1783879/000178387926000167/hood-20260930.htm)\nciteturn23view5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn16view0\",\"pattern\":\"unrecognized\"}); Total lines: 4228\nL1554: We have capitalized SBC expense related to internally developed software of $5 million and $15 million during the three and nine months ended September 30, 2026 compared to $6 million and $17 million for the three and nine months ended September 30, 2025.\nL1555: \nL1556: As of September 30, 2026, there was $453 million of unrecognized SBC expense that is expected to be recognized over a weighted-average period of 1.04 years.\nL1557: \nL1558: 46\nL1559: \nL1560: * * *\nL1561: \nL1562: 【35†Table of Contents】\nL1563: \nL1564: NOTE 14: NET INCOME (LOSS) PER SHARE\nL1565: We present net income (loss) per share using the two-class method. Class A and Class B common stock have identical liquidation and dividend rights, differing only in voting rights; accordingly, undistributed earnings are allocated proportionately and EPS is the same for both classes on an individual and combined basis.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRobinhood 2025 10-K/A (https://investors.robinhood.com/static-files/36353485-5cd1-4eb2-9eb4-6d266f75374b)\nciteturn23view6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 203; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn11view0\",\"pattern\":\"CONDENSED\"}); Total lines: 8655\nNo matching text found for \"CONDENSED\"--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nhood-20260930 (https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1783879/000178387926000167/hood-20260930.htm)\nciteturn23view7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn16view0\",\"pattern\":\"gains on deconsolidation\"}); Total lines: 4228\nL948: As a result, we recognized a gain on deconsolidation of $106 million for the nine months ended September 30, 2026, which relates to the remeasurement of our retained interest in RVI to fair value at the deconsolidation date. The gain was recognized in Other income (expense), net in the unaudited condensed consolidated statements of operations.\nL949: Following deconsolidation, we elected the fair value option under ASC 825-10 to account for our retained interest in RVI, with changes in fair value recognized in Other income (expense), net in the period in which they occur. As of September 30, 2026, the fair value of our retained interest was recorded at $361 million and is included in Other current assets in the unaudited condensed consolidated balance sheets.\nL950: \nL951: Deconsolidation of RVII\nL952: On August 13, 2026, RVII commenced trading on the NYSE in connection with its initial public offering, which closed August 14, 2026. Upon closing, the issuance of common stock in the offering diluted our ownership interest in RVII and resulted in the loss of our controlling financial interest. Accordingly, we deconsolidated RVII and no longer include RVII's assets, liabilities, and results of operations in our consolidated financial statements as of that date forward.\nL953: RHV remains the advisor to RVII and charges a management fee of 2% of RVII's NAV as well as a 20% incentive fee based on realized capital gains.\nL954: In connection with the deconsolidation, we derecognized all assets and liabilities of RVII at their carrying values of $25 million, net, as of August 14, 2026. Upon the loss of our controlling financial interest, we remeasured the fair value of our retained interest in RVII at a fair value of $26 million as of August 14, 2026.\nL955: The fair value of our retained interest in RVII was determined based on the closing market price of RVII common stock on August 14, 2026, a Level 1 input under the fair value hierarchy. Refer to Note 8 - Investments and Fair Value Measurement for further information.\nL956: As a result, we recognized a gain on deconsolidation of $1 million for the three and nine months ended September 30, 2026, which relates to the remeasurement of our retained interest in RVII to fair value at the deconsolidation date. The gain was recognized in Other income (expense), net in the unaudited condensed consolidated statements of operations.\nL957: Following deconsolidation, we elected the fair value option under ASC 825-10 to account for our retained interest in RVII, with changes in fair value recognized in Other income (expense), net in the period in which they occur. As of September 30, 2026, the fair value of our retained interest was recorded at $23 million and is included in Other current assets in the unaudited condensed consolidated balance sheets.\nL958: \nL959: 27\nL960: \nL961: * * *\nL962: \nL963: 【35†Table of Contents】\nL964: \nL965: NOTE 5: GOODWILL AND INTANGIBLE ASSETS\nL966: \nL967: Goodwill\nL968: The carrying amount of goodwill for the period indicated was as follows:\nL969: \nL970:  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\nL971: (in millions)  |  | Carrying Amount\nL972: As of December 31, 2025  |  | $  | 385   |\nL973: Additions  |  | 143   |\nL974: Measurement period adjustment  |  | (6)  |\nL975: Foreign currency translation adjustment  |  | (7)  |\nL976: As of September 30, 2026  |  | $  | 515   |\nL977: \nL978: There was no impairment of goodwill during the nine months ended September 30, 2026.\nL979: \nL980: Intangible Assets\nL1471: Gains and losses on the public stock token derivatives are largely offset by gains and losses on the securities we hold to back the tokens. For the three and nine months ended September 30, 2026, the losses of the stock token derivatives were $7 million and $8 million, respectively, which were largely offset by gains on the underlying securities held to back the tokens.\nL1472: \nL1473: NOTE 13: COMMON STOCK AND STOCKHOLDERS’ EQUITY\nL1474: \nL1475: Preferred Stock\n"
